From e0052f92803f2ccd3c034abd67dfe703f0ffeabb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luca Bruni <luca.bruni@amd.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(AMDGPU): end the wave after llvm.trap when no trap
 handler runs

llvm.trap (__builtin_trap, a failed device assert) lowers to a bare
s_trap 2 on targets with the AMDHSA trap handler ABI. Where no trap handler
is installed (for example gfx9 on Windows with a KMD that refuses the
set-trap-handler escape) s_trap is a no-op and the wave runs whatever
follows: garbage results, engine resets, a poisoned GPU.

Follow the trap with the existing ENDPGM_TRAP fallback (s_endpgm). It is
unreachable when a handler exists, so behavior there is unchanged.

Checked: the 28 trap tests (6 regenerated) and all 5145 CodeGen/AMDGPU tests
pass; on gfx90c, __builtin_trap and assert now stop all 64 lanes at the trap
and the GPU stays healthy.
