 .../si-unify-exit-multiple-unreachables.ll    |  25 ++-
 llvm/test/CodeGen/AMDGPU/trap-abis.ll         |  18 +-
 .../AMDGPU/vgpr-spill-placement-issue61083.ll |   8 +-
 10 files changed, 226 insertions(+), 75 deletions(-)

diff --git a/llvm/docs/AMDGPUUsage.rst b/llvm/docs/AMDGPUUsage.rst
index 221b9d25e2b7..ac52b23d84da 100644
--- a/llvm/docs/AMDGPUUsage.rst
+++ b/llvm/docs/AMDGPUUsage.rst
@@ -20243,6 +20243,11 @@ supports the ``s_trap`` instruction. For usage see:
 - :ref:`amdgpu-trap-handler-for-amdhsa-os-v3-table`
 - :ref:`amdgpu-trap-handler-for-amdhsa-os-v4-onwards-table`
 
+The ``s_trap 0x02`` emitted for ``llvm.trap`` is followed by ``s_endpgm``. It is
+not reached when the trap handler is installed. If a runtime does not install
+one, ``s_trap`` is a no-op, and the ``s_endpgm`` terminates the wavefront instead
+of letting it execute whatever follows the trap.
+
   .. table:: AMDGPU Trap Handler for AMDHSA OS Code Object V2
      :name: amdgpu-trap-handler-for-amdhsa-os-v2-table
 
